From 19f5041ac63817a2259b00b91b1d653e7fac7cee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:02:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: structure wallet availability and startup parameter
 decisions

Give wallet-disable, ignored wallet argument, blocksonly broadcast choice,
and wallet-not-compiled diagnostics stable event identities. Reuse the
existing source-function and wallet string fields; preserve all guards,
early returns, SoftSetBoolArg decisions, Info levels and readable text.
No new key material, secrets or extra option values are logged.

The real wallet-enabled startup fixture starts disabled with an ignored
wallet argument, then restarts blocksonly without loading any wallet and
checks unchanged RPC behavior plus typed JSON/text. The wallet-OFF static
producer requires separate build coverage; it is not executed by this test.

Scripted diff (ast-grep-py==0.51.0, from the commit's parent):
/private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/wallet-startup-diagnostics.json --apply

git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style '{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}' HEAD -- src/wallet/init.cpp src/dummywallet.cpp

Handwritten: focused functional fixture; no production support changes.
